From d8801fec5a641c17f25d9ed9e46f8f03155f9a37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] custom_io: generator support for custom pad cells

- scripts/parse_config.py: CUSTOM_PADS table (cell -> core-side pins),
  checked against the ports of magic/custom_io/<cell>.mag, used in all
  four places that switch on the pad type.  One core signal and one
  wrapper port <signal>_<pin> per pad pin.
- scripts/custom_io.tcl (new): label_right_custom / label_left_custom,
  Via2 on the pad's M2 pin stub + 0.29 um Metal3 strap + port label,
  sourced by gen_padframe_template.tcl (+ addpath custom_io).
- scripts/run_update_frame_custom_io.sh (new, make frame-custom-io):
  erases the stale hand-made pad-edge copies in chipalooza_frame.mag in
  the bands of custom pads, before make wrappers.
- netlist/schematic/custom_io.spice (new) and one readnet line each in
  validate/run_lvs_padframe.sh and validate/run_lvs_ocd_chipalooza.sh.

Foundry pad types and other slots: make config output unchanged;
padframe and wrapper .mag unchanged except port index renumbering.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XU3KH5LbmFCchnNvtB8nAZ
